                  <fr:day>3</fr:day>
                </fr:date>
                <fr:uri>https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-0018/</fr:uri>
                <fr:display-uri>dhsorens-0018</fr:display-uri>
                <fr:route>/dhsorens-0018/</fr:route>
                <fr:title text="Summary of Work and Projects">Summary of Work and Projects</fr:title>
                <fr:meta name="toc">true</fr:meta>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>
    Since early 2018 I have held various roles in crypto, working mostly in research and <fr:link href="/dhsorens-000X/" title="Formal Specification and Verification" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-000X/" display-uri="dhsorens-000X" type="local">formal verification</fr:link>.
    My original interests in crypto were in consensus algorithms and formal verification frameworks for verifying smart contracts. When I started, those frameworks and tools were in their infancy, <fr:link href="/dhsorens-001D/" title="The K Framework" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-001D/" display-uri="dhsorens-001D" type="local">K Framework</fr:link> being the only tool at the time to my knowledge that was production-ready for actual smart contracts.

    Over time, I became interested in the financial applications of <fr:link href="/dhsorens-000Y/" title="Smart Contracts" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-000Y/" display-uri="dhsorens-000Y" type="local">smart contracts</fr:link> and I did my <fr:link href="/dhsorens-phd/" title="PhD in Formal Methods" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-phd/" display-uri="dhsorens-phd" type="local">PhD</fr:link> in verification strategies for financial <fr:link href="/dhsorens-000W/" title="Smart Contract Design, Specification, and Verification" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-000W/" display-uri="dhsorens-000W" type="local">smart contracts</fr:link>.

    Along the way, I became deeply interested in type theory and <fr:link href="/dhsorens-000B/" title="Interactive Theorem Provers" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-000B/" display-uri="dhsorens-000B" type="local">proof assistants</fr:link>, and these days am interested broadly in theorem-proving, <fr:link href="/dhsorens-notes/" title="Notes" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-notes/" display-uri="dhsorens-notes" type="local">whether applied to software or formalized maths</fr:link>.

    In my day-to-day, I still do a lot of work in the design, construction, and formal verification of smart contracts.
</html:p>
                <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
                  <fr:frontmatter>
                    <fr:authors>
                      <fr:author>
                        <fr:link href="/dhsorens/" title="Derek Sorensen" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens/" display-uri="dhsorens" type="local">Derek Sorensen</fr:link>
                      </fr:author>
                    </fr:authors>
                    <fr:date>
                      <fr:year>2025</fr:year>
                      <fr:month>9</fr:month>
                      <fr:day>3</fr:day>
                    </fr:date>
                    <fr:uri>https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-0019/</fr:uri>
                    <fr:display-uri>dhsorens-0019</fr:display-uri>
                    <fr:route>/dhsorens-0019/</fr:route>
                    <fr:title text="Pre-PhD (2017-2019)">Pre-PhD (2017-2019)</fr:title>
                  </fr:frontmatter>
                  <fr:mainmatter>
                    <html:p>
    I started working in crypto during the two years between my <fr:link href="/dhsorens-msc/" title="MSc in Algebraic Topology" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-msc/" display-uri="dhsorens-msc" type="local">MSc</fr:link> and my <fr:link href="/dhsorens-phd/" title="PhD in Formal Methods" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-phd/" display-uri="dhsorens-phd" type="local">PhD</fr:link>.
    My first job was at a small, Utah-based crypto startup called Pyrofex, which was mostly providing consulting services to the <fr:link href="https://github.com/dhsorens/rchain" type="external">RChain co-op</fr:link> at the time.
    I was tasked with <fr:link href="https://github.com/dhsorens/rholang" type="external">building the formal semantics for rholang</fr:link>, the smart contracting language on RChain, in <fr:link href="/dhsorens-001D/" title="The K Framework" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-001D/" display-uri="dhsorens-001D" type="local">K Framework</fr:link> in order to formally verify rholang contracts down the line.
</html:p>
                    <html:p>
    RChain, famously, encountered sudden and urgent financial problems because of a questionable set of decisions from the co-op's president, Greg Meredith, which necessitated a split between RChain and Pyrofex.
    We then pivoted to consensus-level research, designed our own layer-one blockchain and <fr:link href="/docs/Casanova.pdf" type="external">consensus protocol</fr:link>.
</html:p>
                    <html:p>
    Sadly, we ran out of money, and I had to look for a new job for the few months before my PhD started.
